<item><title>Forward Notification of Upcoming North Coast Line North Culvert Replacement</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Forward Notification only - please await tender release on 13th January 2027 before initiating queries about the project.<br /><br />The North Coast Line Culvert Renewal Project forms part of Queensland Rail's ongoing program to improve the safety, reliability and resilience of the North Coast Line (NCL). Maintaining the condition and performance of drainage infrastructure is essential to protecting the track formation, managing flood risks and ensuring the ongoing reliability of rail operations.<br /><br />The project involves the replacement of six life-expired corrugated metal pipe (CMP) culverts and grout fill of two CMPs located between 1322.920 km and 1327.880 km on the North Coast Line, within the Nome to Stuart section south of Townsville. The existing culverts have been identified for renewal to address their deteriorating condition and maintain the long-term performance of the corridor's drainage infrastructure.<br /><br />The proposed works involve the removal of the existing culverts and construct...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Rail<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 03/Dec/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP534466<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Railway, Tramway and Track<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 0]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=5d3dc5ec699741688bca83e122874e88s534466sa8d781e850824c0190b34284ab13cf05s5205</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">5d3dc5ec699741688bca83e122874e88</guid>
<pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:22:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Railway, Tramway and Track</category>
</item>
<item><title>RFT000039: Oracle Fusion Cloud Application Support Services.</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Principal is seeking a suitably qualified and experienced Supplier to provide ongoing application management and support services (the Services) for its Oracle Fusion Cloud Applications environment and the integrations connecting it to the Principal's wider application landscape.<br /><br />The Services comprise:<br /><br />•	Level 2 and Level 3 support across the implemented Oracle Fusion Cloud modules, integrations, reports and extensions<br /><br />•	problem management and continuous improvement<br /><br />•	on request management of Oracle's quarterly update cycle, including impact assessment, regression testing and defect remediation<br /><br />•	the service management, security, knowledge transfer and reporting obligations that surround them.<br /><br />Level 1 support and service desk triage are retained by the Principal. Level 4 product support remains with Oracle under the Principal's subscription; the Supplier raises, manages and escalates Oracle Service Requests on the Principal's behalf and ret...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Port of Townsville Limited<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Dec/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP534390<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
