<item><title>Nyah Pavillion Cricket And Active Zone</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Swan Hill Rural City Council (Council) invites suitably qualified and experienced contractors to submit a Tender for the Nyah Pavillion Cricket and Active Zone project. <br /><br />Goals:<br /><br />•	Replace the Nyah & District Cricket Club’s worn-out practice nets with a year-round, all weather indoor facility in the WJ Rose Pavilion.<br /><br />•	Activate the pavilion as a multi-use hub for sport, markets, and community events<br /><br />•	Install free outdoor fitness equipment to expand recreational opportunities in Nyah and Nyah West.<br /><br />•	Maximise use of an underutilised asset and respond to priorities in the Nyah Riverfront Masterplan.<br /><br />•	Ensure that the new facility is accessible for all.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Swan Hill Rural City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 15/Jan/2027 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP534411<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
