<item><title>Cold Chain Monitoring - Bayside</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The procurement is for the implementation of a cloud-based cold chain monitoring system across Bayside Health Service (BHS) to monitor the temperature of medication, vaccine, and pathology storage refrigerators. The solution will replace three separate legacy monitoring systems currently in use: ACR Trendreader (AXIOM), Quirks LogTags, and BMS. The new system will provide continuous 24/7 temperature monitoring, real-time alerts, centralised data access, audit trails, reporting, and regulatory compliance capabilities. The need arises from ageing and unsupported infrastructure, fragmented monitoring processes, incompatibility with newer refrigeration equipment, and increasing clinical and operational risks associated with temperature-sensitive products.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Metro South Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Dec/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP534385<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms, Medical Equipment. & Supplies<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
