<item><title>Mount Morgan Mine General Manager Tiled Roof Refurb</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Natural Resources and Mines, Manufacturing and Regional and Rural Development is seeking suitably qualified and experienced contractors to undertake roof refurbishment works to the General Manager's Residence at the heritage-listed Mount Morgan Mine Site, located approximately 32 km south-east of Rockhampton.<br /><br />The General Manager's Residence, constructed in 1951, forms part of the Queensland Heritage Register-listed Mount Morgan Mine Site (QHR ID 600751). The building comprises timber-clad walls on a brick plinth and piers with a hipped terracotta-tiled roof. While the building remains structurally sound, maintenance works are required to preserve the asset and its heritage values.<br /><br />The proposed works focus on refurbishment of the existing terracotta roof. The residence is currently unoccupied. Repair, replacement or refurbishment of attached metal roofing elements is excluded from the scope, and no allowance has been made for these works.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Dept Natural Res Mines Manufact Regional Rural Dev<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 10/Dec/2026 10:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP534329<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint.<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
