<item><title>MBCC-581 - Management and Operation of Aquatic Facilities</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> City of Moreton Bay invites submissions from suitably qualified and experienced organisations to manage and operate one or more of Council's aquatic venues.<br /><br />City of Moreton Bay operates one of Queensland's largest local government aquatic networks, comprising a diverse mix of regional and local venues that deliver swimming, aquatic recreation, learn to swim programs, health and fitness services, and opportunities for community connection.<br /><br />Collectively, the venues attract more than 1.5 million visits annually and play an important role in promoting active lifestyles, water safety, community wellbeing and participation across the region. The network includes both year-round and seasonal venues, ranging from major regional aquatic and leisure centres to local community pools servicing smaller townships.<br /><br />Council is seeking innovative, community focused and commercially capable partners that can deliver safe, efficient and high-quality aquatic services while supporting Council's vi...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Moreton Bay<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Jan/2027 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533806<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Chemicals, Biochemical, Gas, Cleaning Services, Equip, Supplies, Mechanical Plant, Equip, Services, Real Estate & Property Services, Sport, Recreation Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 11]]></description>
