<item><title>Adult Mental Health Step Up Step Down and Community Care Unit Services [CHHHS]</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Cairns and Hinterland Hospital and Health Service (CHHHS) seek offers from appropriately qualified, experienced and recovery focused Non-Governmental Organisations (NGO’s), for the provision of contemporary Non-Clinical psychosocial rehabilitation services in community bed-based facilities which will ensure Consumers with a severe and<br /><br />persistent mental illness or disorder aged 18 years to 65 years receive the relevant treatment required, in a timely manner.<br /><br />A distinctive feature is the collaborative operational relationship between the Customer and the Supplier in the delivery of the multidisciplinary, quality, recovery focused Services. In delivering adult Community Bed-Based Services and, as part of the Models of Service, the Customer will partner with the Supplier to provide the necessary recovery-based treatment, support and care to Consumers.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Health<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533688<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Healthcare Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 11]]></description>
