<item><title>Surplus Vacant Land Strategy 2.0 Consultancy Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> *Please also download the 3 attachments relating to this request. <br /><br />SERVICES REQUIRED<br /><br />Council is seeking a suitably qualified and experienced consultant to provide multidisciplinary advisory services and independent advice to support the development of Council’s Surplus Vacant Land Strategy 2.0.<br /><br />The consultancy will support Council at key stages of the project, including review and validation of the assessment methodology, portfolio assessment and options analysis, prioritisation, targeted assessment of complex or priority landholdings, and development of the final Strategy and implementation roadmap.<br /><br />The engagement is intended to supplement Council’s internal capability with specialist expertise where required, while supporting a consistent, evidence-based and defensible approach to the assessment of Council’s land portfolio and development of strategic recommendations.<br /><br />Council will retain responsibility for project management, development and maintenance...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533527<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Tamara White Email: twhite@chrc.qld.gov.au Tel: (07) 4988 7292<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Legal Services, Management Advisory Services, Real Estate & Property Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
