<item><title>Charleville Airport - Airside Resealing and Line Marking</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Murweh Shire Council invites tenders for Airside Resealing and Line Marking at Charleville Airport, a certified aerodrome that stays operational throughout.<br /><br />Scope (three Separable Portions, each with sprayed seal and line marking):<br /><br />- Main Apron (RPT apron, Bays 1 and 2): approx. 7,555 m2<br /><br />- Taxiway E: approx. 8,000 m2<br /><br />- GA Apron: approx. 15,808 m2<br /><br />Sprayed seal (S15E binder, emulsion and sand lock-down) to the AfPA Airport Sprayed Sealing Specification v2.1. Tenderers must price both alternatives: A (Single/Single 10 mm) and B (14/10 mm Double/Double). Line marking to MOS Part 139.<br /><br />Aircraft operations must not be affected. Work is limited to Approved Work Windows when no scheduled RPT flights operate, with each area handed back FOD-free on time.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Murweh Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 03/Dec/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533383<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
