<item><title>1583-2026Q RFQ - Dams Condition Audit</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Council seeks to appoint a consultant to undertake condition assessments of six Council-recognised dam assets across the municipality. The audit will establish a consistent baseline of asset condition and information, identify defects and safety-related concerns, and provide practical, asset-specific recommendations for inspection, surveillance, maintenance and ongoing asset management.<br /><br />The scope of works is generally as depicted in Appendix A, which includes but is not limited to:<br /><br />•	Review information supplied by Council and prepare an asset-by-asset inspection plan.<br /><br />•	Inspect the six in-scope dams and assess accessible and observable components, including embankments, spillways, inlet/outlet structures, hydraulic components, downstream areas and public interfaces, as applicable.<br /><br />•	Assess and grade condition using Council’s five-point condition grading scale at component level, identify and prioritise defects, record photographs and promptly escalate any immine...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Banyule City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Dec/2026 03:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533400<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
