<item><title>Replacement of EOL Storm Water Pumps and System Upgrade at MSAC</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The purpose of this project is the planned, like-for-like replacement of aging, end-of-life storm water pumps and associated pipework, valves and other surrounding deteriorated framework. Mechanical switchboard selector switches, indicator lights, ammeter and runtime counters will also be replaced as part of this project. <br /><br />Currently, this system is operating beyond its planned mechanical life and overall is in poor condition. To mitigate the risk of failure and facility downtime and restore operational reliability to required standards this project will remove the old assets and supply and install two new pumps. Associated framework, valves and other aging pipework will also be replaced/modified where required.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> State Sport Centres Trust<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533297<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
