<item><title>RFQ2627/005 - Forrest Avenue Wisbey Street Roundabout Detailed Design</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The City is seeking an experienced design consultant to undertake the detailed design of a new roundabout at the intersection of Forrest Avenue and Wisbey Street. <br /><br />The upgrade is being driven by the development of the new South West Aboriginal Medical Service (SWAMS) Health Hub at Jaycee Park. The additional traffic and access demands generated by the facility require the existing intersection to be upgraded to a roundabout to maintain safe and efficient operation for all road users.<br /><br />The City is providing a concept design, which the successful consultant will develop through to a construction-ready detailed design. The design is to address civil works, stormwater drainage, street lighting and service/utility design and coordination, with due consideration given to road safety, construction and whole-of-life cost, and asset lifecycle.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Bunbury<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 02/Dec/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+08:00) Perth time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533261<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Jane Parsons Email: jparsons@bunbury.wa.gov.au Tel: (08) 9792 7018<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Parking, Traffic Services & Equip<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=98c4e3edb006415389060a684000bdc9s533261</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">98c4e3edb006415389060a684000bdc9</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:39:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Architecture, Design, Planning</category>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Engineer, Research, Tech services</category>
<category>Parking, Traffic Services &amp; Equip</category>
</item>
<item><title>Castlemaine Town Hall Electrification Works - HVAC (Re-advertised)</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Scope of works includes to install a new HVAC system for the main hall and remove the existing wall mounted electrical radiate heaters (15 wall units) within main hall and make good. The Preliminaries Specification, Electrical Drawings, Mechanical Drawings, and all attachments, represent the scope of works under the contract.<br /><br />The tender drawings and specifications are not organised on the basis of trades, rather, they are a package that should be read collectively. It is the responsibility of the Contractor to ensure that each subcontractor has all the information relevant to their work. The Contractor shall not be entitled to claim for any cost arising from submitting only part of the tender package to a subcontractor. <br /><br />MANDATORY SITE INSPECTION<br /><br />The site inspection is mandatory for all tenderers. However, Tenderers who attended the previous site inspection are not required to attend a second inspection.<br /><br />10am Tuesday 17 November 2026<br /><br />25 Lyttleton Street, ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Mount Alexander Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 10/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533277<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Mechanical Plant, Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
