<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:48:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Architecture, Design, Planning</category>
<category>Engineer, Research, Tech services</category>
<category>Management Advisory Services</category>
</item>
<item><title>VP527276 Whitsunday Coast Airport - Apron Bay 1 Expansion</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Whitsunday Regional Council (the Principal) owns and operates the Whitsunday Coast Airport (WCA), located at Proserpine, Queensland. As the primary aviation gateway to the Whitsunday region, the airport plays a significant role in supporting tourism, regional economic development, investment, employment opportunities and connectivity for residents, visitors and businesses.<br /><br />The Whitsunday Coast Airport Master Plan (2024) identified forecast growth in aircraft movements, aircraft size and passenger demand, together with the associated infrastructure improvements required to support future airport operations. As part of the implementation of the Master Plan, the Principal is undertaking the Apron Bay 1 Expansion Project to expand the eastern portion of the existing apron, improve operational flexibility and support the accommodation of larger aircraft and future growth in scheduled air transport operation’s (ATO).<br /><br />A Tender Briefing will be held 3.00pm Wednesday, 25th November 2026, meeting ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Whitsunday Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527276<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, ELEC, Lighting, Equip & Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
