<item><title>Stationary &amp; Abandoned Vehicle Management Service, and/or Storage, Release, Disposal &amp;Administration</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) operates the Queensland State-controlled road network and is responsible for managing disruptions that affect the safe and efficient movement of people and goods across Queensland. A key component of this responsibility is the management of stationary and abandoned vehicles that adversely impact road safety, network operations, network capacity, and traffic flow.<br /><br />Stationary and abandoned vehicles can create significant safety risks for road users, emergency responders and road workers, while also contributing to congestion, travel time delays and secondary incidents. These risks are particularly evident on high-speed, high-volume corridors, including motorways, highways, major arterial roads and critical network interchanges throughout South East Queensland.<br /><br />To support safe and efficient operation of the road network, TMR requires service providers capable of delivering timely and effective vehicle management services across the Metropolit...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Transport and Main Roads - INO<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP533121<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Business & Administrative Services, Fleet Servicing & Accessories, Transport, Freight, Logistics<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
