<item><title>CN2027-025 – Water and Wastewater Condition Assessment</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Water and Wastewater Condition Assessment Program is one of the projects being delivered through the Major Capital & Recovery Works Program of Douglas Shire Council (DSC) under contract CN2025-066. The project is supported by the Queensland Reconstruction Authority (QRA) Water Betterment funding.<br /><br />Tropical Cyclone (TC) Jasper crossed the Queensland coast in the vicinity of Wujal Wujal in north Queensland on the evening of the 13th of December 2023. TC Jasper was associated with an extraordinary flooding event causing significant impacts to the region in north Queensland.<br /><br />In the months following TC Jasper (16th of December 2023 to May 2025), pipeline failures increased noticeably against pre-event rates. It is considered that the cause of failure is in part, a result of the events that occurred during TC Jasper, including significant ground movement, prolonged saturation of the soil surrounding buried assets, and significant pressure fluctuation caused by repeated starting and stopping...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Douglas Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 03/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532980<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
