<item><title>Russell Island Amenities Project</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Redland City Council (RCC) is seeking tenders from suitably qualified and experienced contractors to deliver the Russell Island Amenities Renewal Project under a Design and Construct contract. The project is located at 22 High Street, Russell Island and is intended to improve public amenities within the Russell Island town centre through the provision of accessible public toilet facilities, supporting wastewater infrastructure and an expanded outdoor community space adjacent to the Russell Island Library.<br /><br />The Works include, but are not limited to:<br /><br />•	Design and construction of a new prefabricated public amenities facility;<br /><br />•	Design and construction of a dedicated onsite sewage treatment system (OSTS) to service the new amenities facility and the existing Russell Island Library;<br /><br />•	Decommissioning, removal and disposal of the existing library septic tank, absorption trenches and associated wastewater infrastructure;<br /><br />•	Feasibility assessment and preliminary d...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Redland City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531155<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Construction & Operation, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 11]]></description>
