<item><title>Bulloo Shire Council: EOI - External Operation and Management of Council’s Fleet and Plant Workshop</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Bulloo Shire Council operates a well-equipped and well-maintained workshop facility located within the Council depot, providing the infrastructure necessary to support the servicing, maintenance and mechanical repair of Council's vehicle and plant fleet. The workshop is appropriately configured to accommodate both heavy plant and light vehicle maintenance activities and is supported by suitable tooling, equipment, storage areas and workspaces.<br /><br />The facility provides a functional and efficient operating environment, with its layout supporting the effective movement of vehicles, plant, parts and personnel. The workshop's condition and level of equipment reflect a significant investment in fleet maintenance infrastructure and provide Council with the capability to undertake a broad range of servicing and repair activities in-house.<br /><br />As a key operational asset within the depot, the workshop supports the ongoing availability, reliability and maintenance of Council's fleet and plant assets and p...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Peak Services Procurement<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532851<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Peter Morichovitis Email: pmorichovitis@wearepeak.com.au Tel: 0480221578<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Fleet Servicing & Accessories, Mechanical Plant, Equip, Services, Transport, Freight, Logistics<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
