<item><title>Support the design, development, testing, validation of the FarmTechConnect AgTech Adoption program</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Primary Industries (DPI) is seeking supplier/s to provide specialist professional services supporting DPI-led delivery of FarmTechConnect. The supplier may engage subcontractors with relevant specialist expertise and will remain responsible for coordinating and delivering all contracted services and outputs. DPI will retain overall responsibility for program leadership, producer-facing delivery and relationships with project partners.<br /><br />DPI requires a consistent approach that enables extension providers to support producers to identify priority farm business challenges, assess digital readiness, evaluate suitable technologies and return on investment, develop staged adoption plans, and implement and integrate technology into existing production systems. The program must support productivity, profitability and resilience outcomes, with a primary focus on red meat enterprises and application to relevant mixed-farming systems.<br /><br />The supplier will translate the pilot’s findings...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Primary Industries<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 23/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532255<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=271b530debda452082ae053cd27d4672s532255s9b84ae7c1e7b4f3397a4dccd2ceae4fbs1583</link>
