<guid isPermaLink="false">ffaf5bf05a504f33800bdd9543a512fd</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 05:42:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Building Trade, Repairs, Maint.</category>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Fire &amp; Safety</category>
</item>
<item><title>Parkhurst Boundary Fencing</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Primary Industries (Principal) requires a suitably qualified and experienced Contractor to undertake the removal of existing perimeter fencing and the supply and installation of new security fencing and associated gates at the DPI Parkhurst facility. The works include approximately 905 metres of 2.1 metre-high black aluminium spear-top fencing, manual vehicle gates, an automated main entry/exit gate, associated site preparation, access-control integration, testing, commissioning and handover.<br /><br />The successful Contractor will be responsible for the removal and disposal of the existing fencing and the supply, installation, testing, commissioning and handover of the new perimeter fencing and associated gates and access infrastructure.<br /><br />This Tender has a mandatory industry briefing on Thursday, 12 November 2026. Tenderers will meet at: 25 Yeppoon Road, Parkhurst QLD 4702 at 11:00am. Two (2) representatives per company will be permitted to attend. Please register for the site v...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Primary Industries<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532218<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
