<item><title>PAH - Endoscopy Procedure Room Upgrade Project</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This procurement seeks to engage a suitability qualified Principal Contractor to deliver the PAH Endoscopy Procedure Room Upgrade Project within the existing Endoscopy Department at Princess Alexandra Hospital including full design and construction. The works involve the refurbishment and reconfiguration of existing departmental spaces, including the conversion of the current Dirty Utility, Staff Toilet, and adjacent shell office area into a dedicated endoscopy procedure room and associated supporting functions. <br /><br />The scope includes completion of any remaining design development, construction, coordination and management of subcontractors, commissioning, defects management and handover within a live operational hospital environment. The project will deliver a contemporary procedure room designed to support complex endoscopy procedures and will include associated building and engineering services modifications such as:<br /><br />•	Medical gases<br /><br />•	Electrical service<br /><br />•	ICT and co...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Metro South Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 01/Dec/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532129<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 16]]></description>
