<item><title>OIR Statutory Interpretation Training</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Office of Industrial Relations (OIR) is seeking to engage a suitably experienced supplier to develop and deliver Statutory Interpretation training for staff of OIR. <br /><br />The objective of the Statutory Interpretation training is to ensure staff in various roles within our regulators are equipped with the knowledge and skills required to effectively interpret and apply legislation and associated statutory instruments in their role. Robust application of the legislation and statutory instruments will lead to consistent application and increased efficiency and confidence in defendable decisions.<br /><br />It is anticipated the training will be up to 1 full day or 2 x ½ delivered in person or virtually via Microsoft Teams to meet requirements for staff spread across multiple locations and regions. <br /><br />This engagement is for a 3-year term with option for extension.<br /><br />Further details are in the attached Request for Quote<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Office of Industrial Relations<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP532010<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Training & Development<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
