<item><title>Cultural Heritage Management, Arts, Interpretation and Visitor Experience Design Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council invites tenders from suitably qualified and experienced consultants to provide Cultural Heritage Management, Arts, Interpretation and Visitor Experience Design Services across three Council capital projects:<br /><br />Indigenous and Arts Installation Precinct (Beachfront Cultural Walk) – Cultural heritage management, cultural engagement, arts curation, artwork and sculpture design, storytelling, interpretive signage, wayfinding and inclusive visitor experience design.<br /><br />Walking Trails and Tourism Activation Project (including Cultural Welcome Precinct) – Cultural heritage management, negotiation of cultural heritage agreements, construction-phase compliance oversight, arts curation, cultural interpretation, artwork, signage, wayfinding and visitor experience design.<br /><br />Rodeo Grounds New Subdivision – Cultural heritage management, stakeholder engagement, negotiation of cultural heritage agreements and compliance oversight during design and construction.<br...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 27/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531968<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Marcio Fialho Email: marcio.fialho@palmcouncil.qld.gov.au Tel: 0448339292<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Environmental & Heritage Services, Graphical, Photographic & Art, Printing & Distribution Services, Railway, Tramway and Track, Signs & Barriers, Training & Development, Travel & Tourism<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 27]]></description>
