<item><title>Butler Bay Sewage Rising Main Replacement – Design and Construct</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council invites suitably qualified and experienced contractors to submit tenders for the Design and Construction of the Butler Bay Sewage Rising Main Replacement Project (PIASC.2627.BBSRM01) on Palm Island, Queensland.<br /><br />The project involves the replacement of approximately 3 kilometres of existing sewage rising main between Sewage Pump Station 5 (SPS 5) at Butler Bay and Sewage Pump Station 6 (SPS 6), generally following the existing Butler Bay Road corridor.<br /><br />The scope includes engineering investigations, hydraulic and detailed design, pipeline supply and installation, associated SPS 5 refurbishment and SPS 6 connection works, temporary sewage bypass arrangements, testing, commissioning, decommissioning and handover.<br /><br />Council is seeking a fully inclusive, lump-sum Design and Construct solution, with the contractor responsible for design development, construction methodology, materials, freight, mobilisation, workforce accommodation and all associated...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531967<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Marcio Fialho Email: marcio.fialho@palmcouncil.qld.gov.au Tel: 0448339292<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
