<item><title>2920_2026-27_TTB_47 - Gayndah STP Upgrade</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> North Burnett Regional Council (Council) invites suitably qualified and experienced contractors to submit an Offer for the Gayndah Wastewater Treatment Plant Upgrade.<br /><br />The project will rehabilitate and return the existing Pond 2 Rock Filter to operation and improve downstream treatment and disinfection while maintaining treatment plant operations and recycled water supply.<br /><br />The Works comprise rock filter rehabilitation and reinstatement, an additional floating treatment wetland, a new sodium hypochlorite storage and dosing system, and decommissioning and demolition of the existing dosing building following successful commissioning of the replacement system.<br /><br />Council intends to award one contract to a single successful Tenderer covering the complete Works, including the design obligations expressly identified in the Specification, construction, installation, testing, commissioning and handover.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> North Burnett Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531865<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
