<item><title>TVP/26/15 AQUALIFE FEASIBILITY STUDY</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Town of Victoria Park (Town) invites submissions from suitably experienced Respondents to develop a feasibility study, needs analysis and redevelopment options for the possible redevelopment of the Town’s Aqualife facility. <br /><br />This will be achieved by detailed research, analysis of a variety of inputs, confirming alignment with strategic objectives, considering stakeholder needs, completing a range of preparatory assessments and filtering possible options into a shortlist of more promising options through a multi-criteria assessment. <br /><br />The feasibility study will specifically consider the potential for migration of the facilities, assets and services currently provided at the Town’s Leisurelife facility to the Aqualife site.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Town of Victoria Park<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 23/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+08:00) Perth time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531096<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Business & Administrative Services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
