</item>
<item><title>Mattress Processing for Resource Recovery</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Logan City Council (Council) is seeking to establish a Contract with a suitably qualified and experienced Contractor for the provision of Mattress Processing for Resource Recovery (WRR/39/2027).<br /><br />The purpose of the Contract is to maximise resource recovery from end-of-life mattresses and reduce the volume of material disposed of to landfill. At a minimum, the Services include the manual or mechanical deconstruction of mattresses and the separation of ferrous metal from other materials for resource recovery. Council welcomes solutions that maximise the recovery and beneficial reuse of mattress components and support improved environmental outcomes.<br /><br />ENQUIRIES:<br /><br />Any questions and responses shall be collated, documented and distributed to all tenderers to ensure equity and fairness to all respondents.<br /><br />All enquiries in relation to this tender must be submitted via the VendorPanel Online Forum.<br /><br />LODGEMENT OF SUBMISSIONS:<br /><br />Completed responses must be subm...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Logan City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 24/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531117<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 15]]></description>
