<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Expressions of interest are sought from organisations that are commercially focussed on research and development activities with the necessary skills, experience and financial resources to develop the land for its highest and best use.<br /><br />Proposals should be in the form of a preliminary business case (including a concept design) and include details on how the site will be developed and ongoing management models. It is noted that any proposal submitted through this EOI process is to be consistent with the requirements of the proposed amendment of part of the site from Conservation to Community Facilities zone of Redland City Plan 2018.<br /><br />Long term lease tenure will be negotiated with the successful proponent, with applicants encouraged to nominate their preferred terms.<br /><br />Evaluation will be based on achieving optimum use by providing a quality, environmentally responsible research and development model and maximising economic and community benefit. Importantly, this process may also b...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Redland City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 23/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530503<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Environmental & Heritage Services, Healthcare Services, Management Advisory Services, Training & Development<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
