<item><title>Construction of the Warburton (WA) Dialysis Facility</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> NHS (Ngaanyatjarra Health Service), in partnership with Purple House, is seeking a Head Contractor to deliver a Design and Construct (D&C) commission for a new 4-chair, nurse-assisted haemodialysis facility at Warburton, in the Ngaanyatjarra Lands, Western Australia. The facility is to be delivered as a modular building, prefabricated off-site and transported to Warburton for installation and completion, with a 40-year design life.<br /><br />Anticipated works commencement is 22 February 2027, with Practical Completion required by 29 October 2027.<br /><br />The site is located on the Ngaanyatjarra Lands, a remote community in Western Australia. Tenderers must allow for all mobilisation, module transport, accommodation and logistics associated with a remote site of this nature.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Jenarc<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 24/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527543<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 19]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=8b88d34f89cf468da9abae756f3e9f50s527543s50c818bb80c044cab1c37a23ba39eee8s1554</link>
