<item><title>RFQ 2526-033 Ben Boyd Dam Water Tower Asset Upgrade</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council is seeking quotes from qualified entities to undertake works for the renewal of critical mechanical assets within the Ben Boyd Dam Intake Tower, including the removal and replacement of three existing DN450 inlet valves, operating spindles and associated mechanical equipment; removal and replacement of the existing winch, wire rope<br /><br />and lifting system components; provision of commercial diving services; installation of a temporary or permanent lifting system; engineering design and certification; testing, commissioning, site reinstatement and all ancillary works required to deliver a complete operational installation. <br /><br />A non-mandatory pre-tender meeting will be held on Thursday, 22 October 2026 at 9am. Tenderers are requested to confirm, via the VendorPanel forum to the Principal’s Contact Person, that they will attend the pre-tender meeting at least 2 Business Days prior to the nominated date. Additional information is available in the Conditions of Tendering.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Bega Valley Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Nov/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529199<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Marine Transp. Products & Services, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 18]]></description>
